cess is a little different and I  believe it's pronounced lua genesis  first of all who in genesis is defined  as the production of the egg cell or the  ovum ovum is just the science word for  an egg cell this takes place in woman's  ovaries women have thousands of cells  called blue sites and new site from the  picture you can see is the diploid cell  whose sites go through meiosis meiosis  number one that you sight will divide  into two cells but notice how the cell  on the left is different than the cell  on the right just in terms of size  that's because during meiosis number one  when that site goes through meiosis  number one the cytoplasm is not  distributed evenly the sow on the Left  received the bulk of the cytoplasm the  bulk of the organelles the cell on the  right I don't want to say it's empty and  Hollow but it's not going to be a  functional cell those two cells the big  cell the small cell let's look at the  two let's look at the small cell on the  right first the small cell on the right  will go through meiosis number two to  make two more cells now the big cell on  the left will also go through meiosis  number two to make two more cells so  here as we said in the notes meiosis  makes four cells and there you see four  cells but you can see that during  meiosis number two that big cell didn't  divide evenly again this the bigger  green cell on the left has the bulk of  the cytoplasm the bulk of the organelles  the other little cell I don't get I  don't want to say it's hollow and empty  but it will become a non-functional cell  we call these three non-functional cells  by the way polar bodies now that one  large cell on the left it's not an egg  cell yet it will go through the process  called good Genesis and eventually take  on the form of a finalized egg cell  women released different sex hormones  than men the hormones released by males  allows for mana Genesis to occur the  hormone is released by women in their  endocrine system allows an egg cell or  an ovum to be produced through this  final process called booyah Genesis  those three other polar bodies as my  notes say those three other polar bodies  simply dissolve and the one mature ovum  can then begin the journey of the of the  menstrual cycle and so the the reason  for this picture right here is just a  nice little compare and contrast if you  want to pause the video I'm not going to  say much about this but if you want to  pause the video you can see a nice  compare and contrast mitosis on the Left  versus meiosis on the right and for  those you who are in my biology class  again you feel free to pause the video  again and try to answer these questions  here if you're in my biology class pause  the video in and put your answers on a  separate sheet of paper I'd be happy to  meet you before school one day or after  school one day and just go over your  answers with you and see how you did so  pause the video and good luck
 

